      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}\n\nNot sure. As far as I can see, only the MB limit is an issue. The parameters for VRC on Quest were based on the Quest 1, and haven't changed since then, besides MB limits on avatars, but I've only seen 3 utilizing that feature. So still, there at least needs to be a way to bridge the gap between avatars and worlds between PC and Quest, quite literally the only thing between the two versions are Shaders. VRC only has like 6 approved shaders for Quest, even though many are optimized enough to not lag Quest users. Problem is, VRChat doesn't see that. They don't actually review shaders, so at the very least, I want VRChat to just blacklist certain shaders for optimization purposes and that's it. Idiotic that Quest users can't see so many Avatars just because of a Shader or Two.",
