      "value": "@{65a8eafb38e2048b3b26086d|full_name}\n\nThey're built on different platforms only because VRC runs on Android on Quest. Quest could most definitely see the Windows build, but the shaders are the problem. Most Cross-Platform Avatars have Custom Shaders, and Mobile Shaders. Mobile shaders so Quest can view it, and Custom Shaders so PC can view it with added clarity. It is the same avatar. Same exact avatar. The only difference is the shaders. What I'm asking is to essentially allow custom shaders on quest, so they would see the same avatar as PC Users would. Of course, it won't look the exact same, but it would allow Quest and PC users to interact more. After viewing some things, I do realize PC-Only Avatars likely won't automatically port to quest as well, and PC-Only Avatars would still exist. I am simply asking for custom shaders to be implemented into Quest instead of only having 6-8 approved ones.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
