  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hello,\n\nI am a Quest 3 user, and I do not think it is fair with the limitations between Quest and PC. I do not want to have to buy a $1,000 system just to see my friend's avatars, or to even just chill with my friends in a PC only world. So, a suggestion I put up is a Opt-In system. Where Quest users can go into their Privacy Settings, or Avatar settings, and Opt-In to a service where the limitations on Quest are removed. Now, I know why the limitations are there, because of non-optimization issues. However, Imposter avatars now exist, and you can remove the MB limit on quest, which does wonders for Customization, and Avatar Looks in general. Which is why I believe when Quest users Opt-In, they'll have to agree to a thing that would say something along the lines of \"By Opting in to this, you acknowledge that you may experience heavy preformance issues, and more lagging, and you acknowledge that you will see a considerate Frame-Rate drop. You can Opt-Out at any time.\"\n\nI propose this idea so Quest users can Opt-In to this, and by agreeing to it, they acknowledge the risks and possiblities, in exchange for unlocking the entirety of VRChat. This will likely be overlooked, but in any case, thank you for your time.",
